cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "traceaudit: requirements-to-test traceability computed from a repository"
abstract: >-
  Parses numbered requirements from markdown and test identifiers, outcomes and
  requirement claims from a junit XML or pytest collection report, computes the
  bidirectional mapping, and reports untraced requirements, undeclared claims,
  duplicate ids, requirements traced only by skipped or expected-failing tests,
  and a coverage percentage with its denominator stated. Traceability is a
  bookkeeping condition and not evidence of adequacy. Research-grade; not
  flight-qualified, not certified, not approved for operational aerospace use,
  and not a DO-178C or ARP4754A compliance tool.
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-10-10"
license: Apache-2.0
authors:
